Most cats will fetch a ball of paper or something similar when they are in a
playing mood, my point was that I have never seen a cat bring the newspaper
(such cats probably do exist, but they're not common) or anything you didn't
throw in the first place, and I've never seen a cat fetch anything when it
isn't in the mood to fetch things anyway :-) Also, sometimes the cat will dash
after the thrown object as if it was a piece of the most delicious food it has
ever tasted, grab it, run back to you and stop about halfways, dropping the
object and itself onto the floor and casting an amused look at you ("now it's
your turn to come and get it") :-)

